title A record is not the work -- the guard that opens the dead-letter box reads the reasoning drawer, and a lap whose log lands over its parked code turns it green
prompt Autonomous lap. Card open, reds first, rota advanced by hand past a row already read.
think Lap N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 4091, so N mod 5 = 1 -- the air row my previous lap already read. Advanced by hand to row 2, fire, the row that sees: cut and stop. Read its threshold page, Standfast, and the three depths of removal. Fire's subject is the stop that must resume, which turned out to be this lap's whole shape.
think The card's open showed a clean tree and eight stashes. git stash list is the first thing %321 asks a lap to read, and stash@{0} held 494 insertions from my own lap four hours earlier -- a complete sow_allow_reach repair with a 26-leg control, a witness, a roster line, a REDS row and a session log, none of it in the channel.
think Measured before believing: sow_allow_reach_control.sh is absent at HEAD, sow_project.sh writes no receipt, and the scan still carries the single-verdict shape. So the park was real and nothing had recovered it.
think Fetch before booking moved the number. My parked row was %506; Patchouli published %506 for Weave.annotate while my work sat in the stash. reds_spine_derive_scan --next read 508, so the row keeps its stamp 20260906.162327 and takes the number %508 -- which is the derived-spine law working exactly as written: the key is the stamp, the number is a view the anointed remote allocates.
think Then the fire question, asked of the instrument rather than of the stash: Patchouli landed stash_record_scan.sh an hour ago and it named my record correctly. So what would it say once that record landed?
obs It says verdict=ok. The scan counts one thing -- a session log -- because every lap writes one, and the proxy parts from its subject exactly when a lap's log lands while its code does not.
obs Measured across the whole box: four files in three round-open stashes, 258 lines, and not one of them raises records by one -- three stashes whose every record reads landed, so the reading said nothing about them at all. The live orphans=5 counts a fifth, my own shelf landed under the name its renumbering gave it, which is the honest false positive the design names. stash@{6} holds agent_jail_control.sh (141 lines) and mount_namespace_probe.sh (44), the pen and the probe that authorize %446's skip, while tools/ag/agent_jail_witness.sh -- the guard those two were written for -- had already landed without them. That stash's own log reads landed:worktree, so the scan said nothing about the stash at all.
think The repair goes inside the landed guard rather than beside it: a second meter over one box is how two meters come to disagree, which is %505's own lesson from this morning. The scan now walks every NON-record path and asks it the same question by the same probe.
obs The two sets are disjoint on purpose -- a record is never also an orphan -- so records and paths partition the box and no file is reported twice under two names. paths = orphans + unread, proven on real numbers in the pen rather than asserted in the arithmetic.
obs unread earns a printed line as well as a count. A file the scan looked at and could not answer for is a different thing from a file it never saw, and all mode promises every path; leaving unread silent broke that promise, which one control leg caught on its first run.
obs Reported rather than gated, and the reason is not caution. unlanded=0 reads zero on every tree because a record belongs in the channel everywhere; an orphan COUNT is a per-checkout fact, so a ceiling measured here would red a ship for merely parking more work. A file landed under a different NAME reads as an orphan too -- my own shelf does, renamed rows-506 to rows-508 in this very lap.
obs fleet_round_open.sh reads both drawers out of ONE scan run, so naming the second costs the open nothing and %291 stays honest: the gate keeps the meaning six ships grep for.
think Proof by what it can tell apart rather than by prose: run the new 51-leg control against the elder scan copied out of HEAD and it reads 41 pass, 10 fail. Ten legs bite.
obs Reds first found a live one at the cold open beneath all this: index_row_bound RED, two stamps carried twice on today's shelf and one misordering -- %440's ninth firing, a rebase re-applying updated rows above their stale twins. The ledger decided which copy was right: the rows naming %504 and %505 match REDS.md, the ones naming %506 and %507 named other rows entirely.
loom roster=cold_open guards=151 red=3 wall_s=1240 tree_moved=no
loom control=stash_record legs=51 fail=0 elder_pass=41 elder_fail=10
loom control=sow_allow_reach behaviors=26 pens=6 fail=0
loom box=this_tree stashes=7 records=6 unlanded=0 paths=46 orphans=5 unread=41
obs RECOVERED FROM THE DEAD-LETTER BOX on 20260906, by the lap that grafted this reading onto the landed room. The log stood in stash@{0} and on no ref, which is exactly the gate it was written to describe.
obs THE ROOM MOVED UNDER THIS LAP. Between the stash and the landing, `tools: every file in the room its own name says` carried stash_record's three files from the f letter room into s, and a peer's %507 repair rewrote the scan's ref reading underneath. The graft was clean in both directions -- the parked body held the peer's park exclusion already, so landing it added the path walk and changed no reading the peer had made.
file tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_scan.sh walks every non-record path a stash holds; orphans, unread and paths printed beside the record gate, which does not move
file tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_control.sh 35 legs to 51, the new ones in their own pen so every number is absolute; the record landed alone to show ok standing over orphans=1
file tools/s/stash_record_witness.rish asserts the path walk is present at all, since a vanished walk answers orphans=0 on every tree forever (%463)
file tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh names both drawers at the open from one scan run
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the stash_record note says what the second reading is and why it reports rather than gates
file tools/fixtures/s/sow_allow_reach_scan.sh restored from the park and renumbered %506 to %508; refuses stale and unprovenanced projections by name
file tools/fixtures/s/sow_project.sh restored; reads HEAD before the copy and writes seed/.sow-projection.log after it
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh restored; the seed_projection probe reads whether the projection names THIS commit
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260906.md two stale duplicate rows dropped and one row sorted, closing %440's ninth firing
file construction/ITINERARY.md the BAKERY account replaced; the stale %499 block folded to the shelf that already held it word for word
recommend check in (Keaton) -- the fifth firing of the card's own question, and this time it cost a landing rather than an hour: my row was %506 when I parked it and %508 when I landed it, because a peer spent the number while my work sat in a stash no reader could see. An OPEN row carrying a claim, a seat and a stamp at START would have held both. The lap that follows is agent-doable and named: land the four standing orphans, %446's pen and probe first.
